{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Exponent.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Exponent.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"zero exponent zero exponent","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Exponent.md","fileName":"Zero Exponent.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Zero Exponent","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Exponents and Roots]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Laws of Exponents","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Exponent.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Exponent.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"zero exponent zero exponent","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Exponent.md","fileName":"Zero Exponent.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Zero Exponent","heading":"Zero Exponent","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For any nonzero base (a), a zero exponent is defined by\n\n$$a^0=1.$$\n\nThis definition keeps the [[Laws of Exponents]] consistent. Dividing a power by itself gives both (a^n/a^n=1) and (a^{n-n}=a^0), so the results agree when (a\\neq0).\n\nThe restriction matters because the quotient argument would divide by zero when (a=0). Elementary algebra therefore leaves (0^0) without the same interpretation rather than treating the zero-exponent rule as unconditional.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Laws of Exponents","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Exponent.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Exponent.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"zero exponent zero exponent","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Exponent.md","fileName":"Zero Exponent.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Zero Exponent","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Laws of Exponents","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}